{
  "title": "Persistent Symptomatic HFrEF When MRA Therapy Is Unsafe",
  "subtitle": "Selecting adjunctive therapy based on symptoms, contraindications, and guideline strength",
  "guideline_sources": [
    "2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Guideline for the Management of Heart Failure"
  ],
  "key_point": "In self-identified Black patients with NYHA class III-IV HFrEF despite optimal therapy, fixed-dose hydralazine-isosorbide dinitrate is recommended when an MRA cannot be safely initiated. [1]",
